The numbers is a list of 0 and 10.
The slack is 2.
The last is the last position of numbers.
The lowest is item 0 of numbers.
The highest is item 0 of numbers.
For every spot from 1 to last.
If item spot of numbers is less than lowest, set lowest to item spot of numbers.
If item spot of numbers is more than highest, set highest to item spot of numbers.

The spread is highest minus lowest.
Set spread to spread minus 2 times slack.
If spread is less than 0, set spread to 0.
Show spread.
